          {
            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 78058,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Let's learn a new concept which explains how variables keep track of things like adding or removing dollars from a wallet.</p><webview version=\"2\" visible-if=\"always\" content=\"&lt;!doctype html&gt;&#xA;&lt;html&gt;&#xA; &lt;head&gt;&#xA;  &lt;style&gt;&#xA;   button {&#xA;    background-color: darkBlue;&#xA;    /* Green */&#xA;    border: none;&#xA;    border-radius: 8px;&#xA;    color: white;&#xA;    text-align: center;&#xA;    text-decoration: none;&#xA;    display: inline-block;&#xA;    font-size: 14px;&#xA;    padding: 6px 12px;&#xA;    margin: 0 12px 0 0;&#xA;   }&#xA;  &lt;/style&gt;&#xA; &lt;/head&gt;&#xA; &lt;body&gt;&#xA;  &lt;h1&gt;Wallet: &lt;strong&gt;$&lt;span id=&quot;amount&quot;&gt;15&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;  &lt;button onclick=&quot;add()&quot;&gt;Add $1&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;  &lt;button onclick=&quot;remove()&quot;&gt;Remove $1&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;  &lt;script&gt;&#xA;   let wallet = 15;&#xA;   let amountCounter = document.getElementById('amount');&#xA;   &#xA;   function add() {&#xA;    wallet += 1;&#xA;    amountCounter.innerHTML = wallet;&#xA;   }&#xA;   &#xA;   function remove() {&#xA;    wallet -= 1;&#xA;    amountCounter.innerHTML = wallet;&#xA;   }&#xA;  &lt;/script&gt;&#xA; &lt;/body&gt;&#xA;&lt;/html&gt;\" /></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Assigning a value",
            "id": 78057,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we create a variable, we <strong>assign</strong> it a value, like assigning <code>3</code> to <code>wallet</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"3\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>When we create a variable, we <strong>assign</strong> it a value. Give <code>wallet</code> a value so the code prints <code>3</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"!=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"3\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Self-assigning a value",
            "id": 78056,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><strong>Self-assignment</strong> is when we set a variable to its own value. For example, we can set <code>wallet</code> to its value <code>3</code> with <code>wallet = wallet</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"19\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"26\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"3\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>wallet</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>wallet</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p><strong>Self-assignment</strong> sets a variable to its own value. Build the second line so <code>wallet</code> keeps its value and the code prints <code>4</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"=\" /><text value=\" \" /><text value=\"wallet\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print\" /><text value=\"(\" /><text value=\"wallet\" /><text value=\")\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"11\" endIndex=\"17\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"3\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"4\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>, followed by <code>wallet</code>, and finally <code>wallet</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Incrementing numbers",
            "id": 78055,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Because we can self-assign variables, we can increase or decrease variables set to numbers. Try increasing <code>wallet</code> with <code>wallet = wallet + 1</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet + \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"3 + 1\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"4\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>wallet + 1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Self-assignment lets us change a number. Increase <code>wallet</code> by one so the code prints <code>4</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet + \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"20\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"wallet - 1\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"wallet + 3\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"4\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>wallet + 1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Why self-assigning matters",
            "id": 78053,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Self-assigning variables let us track data that changes over time. For example, a user might add <code>2</code> dollars to a wallet and then remove <code>1</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet + \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet - \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"29\" endIndex=\"30\" /><option startIndex=\"49\" endIndex=\"50\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"4\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>2</code>, followed by <code>1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Self-assignment lets us track a changing value. Starting from <code>3</code>, first add <code>2</code>, then take away <code>1</code>, so the code prints <code>4</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet + \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"wallet = wallet - \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(wallet)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"28\" /><option startIndex=\"47\" endIndex=\"48\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"4\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>+</code>, followed by <code>-</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Self-assigning strings",
            "id": 78054,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Variables set to strings work the same way. Try setting <code>name</code> to <code>name + \" John\"</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Account name: &quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name = name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; Elton&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name = name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; John&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(name)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"54\" endIndex=\"58\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"Account name:  Elton John\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>name</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Assigning a value",
            "id": 78052,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What value does this code assign to the <code>speed</code> variable?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"speed = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>0</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>speed</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>0</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>A later condition checks <code>speed == 0</code>. Based on this assignment, what does that comparison return?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"speed = \" /><text value=\"0\" class=\"number\" /></content></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>True</code>, because <code>speed</code> stores <code>0</code>.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>False</code>, because <code>speed</code> stores its own name.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">An error, because <code>0</code> cannot be assigned to a variable.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>True</code>, because <code>speed</code> stores <code>0</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Self-assigning a value",
            "id": 78051,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display in the console?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"speed = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"speed = speed\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(speed)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"100\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>100</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>5</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>100</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does this code still display <code>100</code> after the second assignment?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"speed = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"speed = speed\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(speed)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"100\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The second assignment stores the current value of <code>speed</code> back in <code>speed</code>.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Assigning a variable to itself resets it to its first value.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Python ignores every assignment that uses the same variable on both sides.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The second assignment stores the current value of <code>speed</code> back in <code>speed</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Incrementing numbers",
            "id": 78050,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display in the console?  </p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"speed = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"speed = speed + \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(speed)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"101\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>101</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>100</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>101</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>How does the second line make the console display <code>101</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"speed = \" /><text value=\"100\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"speed = speed + \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(speed)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"101\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">It reads <code>100</code>, adds <code>1</code>, then stores <code>101</code> in <code>speed</code>.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">It joins the digits <code>100</code> and <code>1</code>, then stores <code>1001</code>.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">It calculates <code>101</code> but leaves <code>100</code> stored in <code>speed</code>.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">It reads <code>100</code>, adds <code>1</code>, then stores <code>101</code> in <code>speed</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Why self-assigning matters",
            "id": 78063,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why is self-assigning such a powerful programming concept?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Because it lets us track data that changes over time</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Because it helps us create comparisons</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Because it lets us track data that changes over time.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Self-assignment is powerful because it lets us track data that changes over time.</p><p>A game adds <code>points</code> to the current <code>score</code> after each round. Which line tracks the new total?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>score = score + points</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>score == score + points</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>score = points</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>score = score + points</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Self-assigning strings",
            "id": 78049,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display in the console?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Joanne&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name = name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; Rowling&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(name)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Joanne Rowling\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>Joanne Rowling</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>Rowling Joanne</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\"><code>Joanne Rowling</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Why does this code display <code>Joanne Rowling</code> instead of <code>Rowling Joanne</code>?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"name = \" /><text value=\"&quot;Joanne&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"name = name + \" /><text value=\"&quot; Rowling&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(name)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"Joanne Rowling\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The current name is on the left of <code>+</code>, so the new text is added after it.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">The assignment replaces the old name before joining the two strings.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">Self-assignment automatically moves new text to the end, regardless of operand order.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The current name is on the left of <code>+</code>, so the new text is added after it.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Assigning a value",
            "id": 78047,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Assign <code>15</code> to the <code>wallet</code> variable.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"9\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>, followed by <code>15</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Assign <code>15</code> to the <code>wallet</code> variable.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"wallet = \" /><text value=\"15\" class=\"number\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"0\" endIndex=\"6\" /><option startIndex=\"7\" endIndex=\"8\" /><option startIndex=\"9\" endIndex=\"11\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"balance\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"16\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>wallet</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>15</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Self-assigning a value",
            "id": 78046,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Give <code>likes</code> a value so that <code>5</code> displays in the console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"likes = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"likes = likes\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(likes)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"7\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"5\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>likes</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Give <code>likes</code> a value so that <code>5</code> displays in the console.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"likes = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"likes = likes\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(likes)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"6\" endIndex=\"7\" /><option startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"23\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"+=\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"5\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>=</code>, followed by <code>likes</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Incrementing numbers",
            "id": 78045,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add five to the value of the <code>inventory</code> variable.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"inventory = \" /><text value=\"11\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"inventory = inventory + \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(inventory)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"40\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"5\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"16\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>inventory + 5</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Add five to the value of the <code>inventory</code> variable so the code prints <code>16</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"inventory = \" /><text value=\"11\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"inventory = inventory + \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(inventory)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"27\" endIndex=\"40\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"inventory - 5\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"inventory + 6\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"16\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>inventory + 5</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Why self-assigning matters",
            "id": 78044,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Subtract one from the <code>cards</code> variable's value, then add four.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"cards = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"cards = cards - \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"cards = cards + \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(cards)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"27\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>-</code> followed by <code>1</code> and then <code>+</code>, <code>4</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Starting from <code>3</code>, subtract one from <code>cards</code>, then add four, so the code prints <code>6</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"cards = \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"cards = cards - \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"cards = cards + \" /><text value=\"4\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(cards)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"24\" endIndex=\"25\" /><option startIndex=\"26\" endIndex=\"27\" /><option startIndex=\"42\" endIndex=\"43\" /><option startIndex=\"44\" endIndex=\"45\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"*\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"3\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>-</code>, followed by <code>1</code>, <code>+</code>, and finally <code>4</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
