            "title": "Intro",
            "id": 78242,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Since self-assignment is a powerful tool for building programs, let's learn a few operators that help us write code faster.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Intro 2",
            "id": 78221,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>We know that we can add <code>1</code> to a variable by writing out the variable's name. In this case, let's add one to <code>likes</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"likes = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"likes = likes + \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(likes)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"18\" endIndex=\"23\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>likes</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "+= operator",
            "id": 78240,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Rather than rewriting the variable's name, we can use the <code>+=</code> operator to add a number with <code>sales += 1</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"sales = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"sales += \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(sales)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"15\" /><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>sales</code>, followed by <code>+=</code>, and finally <code>1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Rather than rewriting the variable's name, the <code>+=</code> operator adds a number in one step. Use it so the code prints <code>6</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"sales = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"sales += \" /><text value=\"1\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(sales)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"10\" endIndex=\"15\" /><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"18\" /><option startIndex=\"19\" endIndex=\"20\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"=\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"==\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"6\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>sales</code>, followed by <code>+=</code>, and finally <code>1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "-= operator",
            "id": 78232,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To subtract from a variable's value, we use the <code>-=</code> operator.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"sales = \" /><text value=\"5\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"sales -= \" /><text value=\"3\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(sales)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"validatedInput\" isDefault=\"true\" startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"18\" /></interactions><output><content><text value=\"2\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to type <code>-=</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: += operator",
            "id": 78220,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What does this code display in the console? </p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"marbles = \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"marbles += \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(marbles)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"8\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>8</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>6</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>8</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Which longer assignment would update <code>marbles</code> in the same way as the second line?</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"marbles = \" /><text value=\"6\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"marbles += \" /><text value=\"2\" class=\"number\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(marbles)\" /></content><output><content><text value=\"8\" /></content></output></code><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>marbles = marbles + 2</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>marbles = 2</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>marbles = marbles - 2</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>marbles = marbles + 2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: -= operator",
            "id": 78229,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What operator do we use to subtract a number from a variable's value?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>-=</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>+=</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>-=</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>-=</code> operator subtracts a number from a variable's value and stores the result.</p><p>You write <code>lives - 1</code>, but <code>lives</code> does not change. Which replacement subtracts one and stores the result?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>lives -= 1</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>lives += 1</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>lives = 1</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>lives -= 1</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
